20.4. Other Solutions of Mathieu's Equation
Following Erdelyi [20.14], [20.15], define
20.4.1
\varphi_{k}(z)=[e^{i\tau}\cos(z-b)/\cos(x+b)]^{k}\sqrt[k]{J_{k}}(f) where
20.4.2
f=2[q\cos(z-b)\cos(z+b)]^{k}, and J_{A}(f) is the Bessel function of order k; b is a fixed, arbitrary complex number. By using the recurrence relations for Bessel functions the following may be verified:
20.4.3
\frac{d^{2}\varphi_{k}}{dz^2}-2q(\cos2z)\varphi_{k}+q(\varphi_{k-2}+\varphi_{k+2})+k^2\varphi_{k}=0.
It follows that a formal solution of 20.1.1 is given by
20.4.4
y=\sum\limits_{n=-m}^{m}c_{2n}\varphi_{2n+r}

